%%begintext align
%% This march in 6/8 time was first published c. 1730 in Scotland by Daniel Wright,
%% under the title "Lashley's March", but a version can be found in a manuscript collection dating
%% from 1694. It was later scored for harp and uilleann pipes by William Reeve for the pantomine
%% Oscar and Malvina which was first performed in London in 1791.
%% <https://grainnehambly.com/product/highland-march-from-oscar-and-malvina/>
%%endtext


